-- The directives that WALKTHROUGH.md shows.  No assertions: this module only asks questions, and
-- build-walkthrough.py copies what `l4 run` prints for each, so the walkthrough never carries a retyped result.
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Needs the time built-ins.
--
-- The chosen way (W1) is asked through the seat questions of sgbau-seat.l4, which pin both axes inside.
-- Way W2 pins the rule-effective axis directly, with the same rule.
-- Everything between the two BEGIN/END markers at the end is generated from the table of pairs in
-- build-walkthrough.py; edit the generator, not the block.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`
IMPORT `sgbau-first-schedule`
IMPORT `sgbau-act`
IMPORT `sgbau-seat`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `Way W1, as a person with one kind of receiver would ask it`

-- Each helper fixes everything about the person except the kind of receiver and the two days:
-- programmes with pictures and sound are received, sent to anyone with the equipment, and the person operates the
-- receiver at home; they did not install it or sell it, and held no licence.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licensing rule catches a television` MEANS
    `Did I need a licence for my apparatus` conduct reading
        --  kind              pic   snd   anyone  inst   sold   oper
            television        TRUE  TRUE  TRUE    FALSE  FALSE  TRUE

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licensing rule catches a radio` MEANS
    `Did I need a licence for my apparatus` conduct reading
        --  kind              pic   snd   anyone  inst   sold   oper
            radio             TRUE  TRUE  TRUE    FALSE  FALSE  TRUE

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licensing rule catches a satellite dish` MEANS
    `Did I need a licence for my apparatus` conduct reading
        --  kind              pic   snd   anyone  inst   sold   oper
            `satellite dish`  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE    FALSE  FALSE  TRUE

§ `Way W2: the rule-effective axis pinned directly`

-- The same rule as W1, asked with the rule-effective axis pinned to the conduct day instead of the valid-time axis.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`the text, with the rule-effective axis pinned` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` reading
        (`EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` conduct `the version of the First Schedule that governs`)

§ `Left to the clock`

-- The reading day is not pinned: the answer is whatever the machine's clock says today.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`the text, with the reading day left to the clock` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` conduct `the version of the First Schedule that governs`

